# DEPP repository environment example.
#
# This file previously duplicated the api-gateway configuration and drifted out
# of sync with it: it documented AUTH_MODE=dev-header as the only supported mode
# and stated "There is no production-safe mode yet" long after AUTH_MODE=jwt
# landed, and it listed REDIS_URL, JWT_REFRESH_SECRET, TENANT_CONTEXT_KEY,
# API_BASE_URL and POSTGRES_HOST, none of which are read anywhere in
# backend/api-gateway/src.
#
# It is now a pointer rather than a second copy, because one authoritative list
# per service is the only arrangement that cannot drift.
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# api-gateway
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authoritative: backend/api-gateway/.env.example
#
# The service loads .env from its own working directory
# (backend/api-gateway/src/config/env.ts calls dotenv.config()), so a .env at
# the repository root is not read. Copy the gateway example instead:
#
#   cp backend/api-gateway/.env.example backend/api-gateway/.env
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local infrastructure
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# infra/docker-compose.yml reads POSTGRES_DB, POSTGRES_USER, POSTGRES_PASSWORD
# and POSTGRES_PORT from the shell or a root .env, each with a local default.
# These configure the disposable local Postgres container only. They are not
# application configuration and are not used by any deployed environment.
#
# POSTGRES_DB=depp
# POSTGRES_USER=postgres
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
# POSTGRES_PORT=5432
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployed environments
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never derived from this file. Configuration and secrets are injected by the
# deployment mechanism as process environment variables, and secrets are never
# committed or baked into images.
# See docs/architecture/adr/0013-staging-deployment-baseline.md.
